{"kind":"request","text":"LC-2: dap-lending trusts the signed Lending 0.3.0 and Counter 0.3.0.\n\nOutcome: I install Lending 0.3.0 in the hosted `lending-library` room\nafter this head lands and deploys.\n\nThe fact. `apps/room/wrangler.lending.jsonc` trusts the two 0.2.0\nreleases. No room installed either one. The R head changed the\nLending definitions, so the release to install is 0.3.0. I signed\nboth applications from main `c6711b53`. The END act before this\nrequest states each release and packet hash.\n\nWork, modelled on LC-1 commit `206282ba`:\n1. Take the two packets from carrier commit `5cb79ddd`, byte for\n   byte, at `examples/lending/releases/0.3.0/application.dap.json`\n   and `apps/counter/releases/0.3.0/application.dap.json`.\n2. `APPLICATION_TRUST` in `apps/room/wrangler.lending.jsonc` holds\n   exactly the two 0.3.0 rows, with the same publisher and host.\n3. Remove the two 0.2.0 packets and their rows. Decision: no\n   installation uses 0.2.0, and a trust row with no use widens the\n   trusted set. Git history keeps the 0.2.0 packets.\n4. `packages/cli/test/application-release-reproduction.test.ts`,\n   `scripts/format-json.mjs` and `scripts/format-json.test.mjs`\n   name the 0.3.0 paths and version.\n5. Add a short dated section to\n   `notes/2026-11-14-lc1-lending-counter-releases.md` with the two\n   releases, the packet hashes and the main commit.\n\nWitnesses:\n- The reproduction test passes with the 0.3.0 rows. It fails when a\n  row names a release with no committed packet. State that named red\n  once, by a changed row in a scratch copy.\n- The signed identifiers equal current source at the head. If they\n  differ, stop and tell me. The version rule 163de663 then asks for\n  a new version, not a changed packet.\n\nBefore the gate, run the owners that read this configuration:\n`application-release-reproduction.test.ts`, `demo-config.test.ts`,\n`scripts/format-json.test.mjs` and\n`scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs`.\n\nPosition. The head changes no `packages/*/src` path. It rides the\nnext head that takes the gate slot, by the combined route da772676,\nif its paths are disjoint from that head. If the side head already\nruns its gate, LC-2 rides CB-1 and LS-1. Tell me which head carries\nit.\n\nAfter the landing I deploy `dap-lending`. The only plain binding\nthat changes is `APPLICATION_TRUST`. The screen host rows follow in\na later head, after the installation gives its item number.\n\nThis request adds no scope kind, no platform definition name, no\ncapability name or form, no tool family and no record model.","body":{"conditions":"The head lands on main with the gate passed and the checker's approval. Each witness of the request has a test.","target_head":"c6711b53a368d24c1fad2830ea5634c045999ce1","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}